<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<!--
  DDS configuration for the car.

  Two problems this is answering, both measured rather than assumed.

  FastDDS is the default rmw on Humble and it busy-spins on a graph this
  size. UNIST measured it taking a whole core against CycloneDDS idling at
  ~21% on the same node set, and time_trials brings up 21 nodes. That is a
  core we do not have: the particle filter is already scan-limited.

  The bigger one is the network. /scan is published RELIABLE - deliberately,
  because a best-effort publisher starves a reliable subscriber silently -
  and reliable means the publisher retransmits until the subscriber
  acknowledges. Over wifi to a laptop running RViz, that couples the laptop's
  packet loss back into the car: /scan and /tf were seen freezing TOGETHER
  for 0.3 s at a time, growing to 0.35 s over a run. At 3 m/s that is a metre
  of unmodelled motion, which is what the particle filter was jumping on.

  Interfaces are therefore listed explicitly rather than autodetected:

    127.0.0.1   the whole stack is one host; this is the path that matters
    wlan0       the laptop. RENAME IT if `ip -br link` says otherwise.

  enP8p1s0 is deliberately absent. That is the lidar's private 192.168.0.x
  link with nothing on it but the sensor, and discovery traffic there is
  pure waste.

  Used as:
    export RMW_IMPLEMENTATION=rmw_cyclonedds_cpp
    export CYCLONEDDS_URI="file://$HOME/roboracer_unita_ws/cyclonedds.xml"

  If the freezes persist with the laptop connected, the next step is to stop
  sending /scan over the air at all - view it through the foxglove bridge,
  which is one TCP connection that cannot push back into the publisher's DDS
  the way a reliable DDS subscriber does.
-->
<CycloneDDS xmlns="https://cdds.io/config">
    <Domain id="any">
        <General>
            <Interfaces>
                <NetworkInterface address="127.0.0.1" multicast="true"/>
                <NetworkInterface name="wlan0" multicast="true" presence_required="false"/>
            </Interfaces>
            <AllowMulticast>true</AllowMulticast>
        </General>
        <Discovery>
            <ParticipantIndex>none</ParticipantIndex>
        </Discovery>
        <Internal>
            <SocketReceiveBufferSize min="default"/>
            <SocketSendBufferSize min="default"/>
        </Internal>
    </Domain>
</CycloneDDS>
